{"content":"I think the readability of this could be improved. ","codeSuggestion":"  // Do not update the dialog after an await if its source, draft, or save
  // operation has been replaced.
  const isCurrent = () => {
    const state = store.getState();
    const sourceSession = selectCalendarEventSourceSession(state, sessionKey);
    const draft = selectCalendarEventDraftState(state, sessionKey);
    const editSession = selectCalendarEventCreateEditSession(state, sessionKey);

    const hasCurrentSource = sourceSession?.requestId === source.requestId;
    const hasCurrentBaseline = draft?.baseline === baseline;
    const hasCurrentOperation = editSession?.operation?.requestId === requestId;

    return hasCurrentSource && hasCurrentBaseline && hasCurrentOperation;
  };","assessment":"The reviewer proposes named values for the three request checks. Apply this readability change in the owning Save patch while preserving all three checks.","rationale":"isCurrent compares the source request, draft baseline, and Save request. Named values make these separate lifetimes easier to identify. The source, draft, and operation must all remain current after asynchronous work.","recommendation":"change","validation":"Inspected saveCalendarEventEdit, its reducers, and test_staleSuccessAndFailureCannotUpdateReplacement. The hidden reader confirmed changeset 14134074 and the author's reply under this thread. The descendant integration test did not run.","appliedSummary":"","changeSummary":"In the Save patch, refactor isCurrent in mail/components/calendar/content/calendar-event-edit-save.mjs to use named selector results and Boolean checks. Preserve request identity and baseline identity comparisons. Keep this change out of the selected shared Calendar commit.","state":"ready","changeAccepted":false,"changeReverted":false,"changesAmended":false}
